  "color": "#64BDA1",
  "description": "The New Zealand and Freedom Party is a party with a platform largely consists of conservation policy and opposition to COVID restrictions, vaccines, the use of 1080 and fluoridation of water. It was founded in 2015 by Alan Simmons, formerly of the United Future party, and David Haynes, president of the Association of Freshwater Anglers. Following the 2020 pandemic response, many members from the Ban 1080 party joined NZOF. Ban 1080 activist and lawyer Sue Grey is now the elected leader of the party. In 2023, it was part of the wider Freedoms NZ umbrella party, and received 13,025 votes and 0.45% percent of the vote.",
